.TH DIFFVIM 1 "2026-08-12" "diffvim 1.4" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
diffvim \- animate a code diff in vim as if a human were typing it
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B diffvim
.RI [ options ]
.RI <oldfile>
.RI <newfile>

.br
.B diffvim
.RI [ options ]
.B \-\-multi
.RI <old1:new1>
.RI <old2:new2>
\&...

.br
.B diffvim
.RI [ options ]
.B \-\-replay
.RI <file>
.RB [ \-\-from
.IR REV ]
.RB [ \-\-to
.IR REV ]

.br
.B diffvim
.RI [ options ]
.B \-\-git-rev
.IR REV..REV
.RI <file>
[<file> ...]

.br
.B diffvim
.RI [ options ]
.B \-\-diff
.IR FILE
.RB [ \-\-dry-run ]

.br
.B diffvim
.B \-\-version
.br
.B diffvim
.B \-\-help

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B diffvim
opens the old version of a file in vim and animates the transformation into
the new version character by character. The cursor glides between change
locations with smooth ease-in-out acceleration, and only the actually-changed
characters are deleted and re-typed \(em surrounding text is never touched.

After the animation completes (or the user stops it), the buffer is a normal
vim buffer and can be edited, saved, or quit normally. By default the buffer
is marked as not modified so
.B :q
quits cleanly; use
.B --keep-dirty
to leave the buffer modified (then
.B :q!
is required).

Three implementations are available:
.TP
.B diffvim
Bash launcher + embedded Vimscript engine. Uses vim's native
.BR timer_start ()
for async animation. No external dependencies beyond vim 8+. Best for
everyday use.
.TP
.B diffvim-tmux
Bash orchestrator + vim in a tmux pane. Bash sends Ex commands to vim via
.BR tmux\ send-keys .
Requires bash 4+, tmux 3+, vim 8+, diff, sed, awk.
.TP
.B diffvim.pl
Perl orchestrator + vim in a tmux pane. Same architecture as diffvim-tmux
but with pluggable diff parser modules. Requires Perl 5.10+, tmux 3+, vim 8+.

.SH OPTIONS

.SS Core Options

.TP
.BR \-\-speed\  N
Speed multiplier.
.B 0.5
= half speed,
.B 2
= double speed,
.B 5
= 5x speed.
All timing delays are divided by this value.
Also settable via
.B DIFFVIM_SPEED
environment variable.

.TP
.BI \-\-output\  FILE
After the animation completes, write the buffer to
.I FILE
and quit vim. Also works with
.B q
(quit) \(em the buffer is written before stopping.

.TP
.BR \-\-scroll\  zz | zt | zb | none
Scroll the cursor to the specified position during animation:
.RS
.TP 4
.B zz
Center cursor on screen
.TP 4
.B zt
Cursor at top of screen
.TP 4
.B zb
Cursor at bottom of screen
.TP 4
.B none
Don't force scroll (default)
.RE

.TP
.B \-\-multi
Treat arguments as
.I old:new
pairs for multi-file animation. After finishing one file, the animation
transitions to the next.

.TP
.BI \-\-context\  N
Fold unchanged regions longer than 2*N lines, keeping N lines of context
around each hunk. Default: 0 (no folding).

.SS Diff Options

.TP
.BR \-\-parser\  perl | diff2html
(diffvim.pl only) Diff parser to use.
.B perl
uses a pure-Perl LCS algorithm (default, no deps).
.B diff2html
shells out to the
.B diff2html
CLI with
.B \-f json
for line-level parsing.

.TP
.B \-\-word-diff
Use word-level diff instead of char-level. Groups changes by word
(non-space sequences), producing more natural typing patterns.

.TP
.BR \-\-algorithm\  lcs | myers | patience
Line-level diff algorithm.
.B lcs
(default) uses classic LCS dynamic programming.
.B myers
uses O(ND) Myers algorithm (falls back to LCS for correctness).
.B patience
anchors on unique common lines for more human-readable diffs.

.TP
.BI \-\-max-hunk-chars\  N
If a hunk has more than N changed characters, skip the char-by-char
animation and apply the entire hunk instantly.

.TP
.BI \-\-max-word-chars\  N
If a contiguous sequence of modified (non-space) characters is LONGER
than N, apply the whole sequence in one shot with a pause, so the user
can read the change. Sequences <= N are animated character by character.

.TP
.BI \-\-word-pause-ms\  N
Pause in milliseconds after an instant word is applied (only relevant
with
.BR \-\-max-word-chars ).
Default: 150.

.TP
.BI \-\-max-line-len\  N
Warn if any line exceeds N characters (char-level diff may be slow).
Default: 10000.

.TP
.B \-\-semantic-cleanup
Post-process char ops to merge adjacent insert/delete pairs that cancel
out, reducing unnecessary typing.

.TP
.B \-\-indent-aware
Normalize indentation before line-level diff, so lines that differ only
in indentation are treated as "keep" at the line level.

.SS Git Options

.TP
.B \-\-replay
Animate git history for the given file(s). For each commit in the range,
extracts the old version and animates the transformation to the next commit.

.TP
.BI \-\-from\  REV
Git revision to start replay from. Default:
.BR HEAD~5 .

.TP
.BI \-\-to\  REV
Git revision to end replay at. Default:
.BR HEAD .

.TP
.BI \-\-git-rev\  REV..REV
Animate a git commit range using
.I REV..REV
syntax. Shorthand for
.B \-\-replay \-\-from REV1 \-\-to REV2.

.TP
.B \-\-git-blame
Show git blame information for each changed line.

.SS Animation Options

.TP
.B \-\-step-mode
Space advances one char op at a time instead of toggling pause/resume,
for detailed inspection.

.TP
.B \-\-adaptive-timing
Automatically slow down for complex hunks (many char ops close together)
and speed up for simple ones.

.TP
.B \-\-rapid-eol-delete
(Default: on) When the cursor is at the end of the line and all the text
after the cursor is being deleted, apply those deletes in one rapid shot
rather than one char at a time. The single rapid delay is governed by
.B \-\-rapid-eol-delay-ms
and the minimum trailing-char threshold by
.BR \-\-rapid-eol-min-chars .
This makes tail-of-line deletions feel snappy instead of laborious.

.TP
.B \-\-no-rapid-eol-delete
Disable rapid end-of-line deletion. Every character is deleted
individually with
.B DIFFVIM_DELETE_DELAY_MS
between deletes.

.TP
.BI \-\-rapid-eol-delay-ms\  N
Delay in milliseconds for a rapid end-of-line deletion (default: 80).
The whole trailing run of deletes is applied in one shot, followed by this
delay. Lower values make tail deletions feel faster.

.TP
.BI \-\-rapid-eol-min-chars\  N
Minimum number of trailing characters required to trigger rapid end-of-line
deletion (default: 3). Runs shorter than this are animated char by char.

.TP
.B \-\-keep-dirty
Leave the buffer marked as modified after the animation finishes (or after
the user presses
.BR q ).
By default diffvim runs
.B :set nomodified
so that
.B :q
quits cleanly; with
.B \-\-keep-dirty
the user must type
.B :q!
to quit. Useful when you want vim's normal "unsaved changes" protection
to remain active.

.TP
.B \-\-highlight-word
Highlight the word at the cursor position before each delete or insert op
is applied. Finer-grained than
.BR \-\-highlight-hunk :
instead of highlighting the whole hunk region (a line range),
.B \-\-highlight-word
highlights just the token (maximal run of non-whitespace chars) that is
about to change. Useful for following the animation on long lines where
the eye needs help locking onto the exact word being modified.

The highlight is shown for
.B \-\-highlight-word-duration-ms
milliseconds (default: 300), then cleared. Words shorter than
.B \-\-highlight-word-min-chars
(default: 2) are not highlighted.

.TP
.BI \-\-highlight-word-color\  COLOR
Vim highlight group for word highlighting. Default:
.BR Search .
Also:
.BR Visual ,
.BR IncSearch ,
.BR DiffAdd ,
.BR DiffDelete ,
.BR DiffChange .

.TP
.BI \-\-highlight-word-duration-ms\  N
Word highlight duration in milliseconds. Default: 300. Lower values make
the highlight flash briefly; higher values leave it visible longer (useful
with
.B \-\-step-mode
or slow animation speeds).

.TP
.BI \-\-highlight-word-min-chars\  N
Minimum word length (in characters) to trigger word highlighting.
Default: 2. Words shorter than this are not highlighted (they change too
fast to be worth the visual flash). Set to 1 to highlight every single-char
change.

.TP
.B \-\-sign-column
Show
.B +/-
signs in vim's sign column to indicate deleted/added lines.

.TP
.B \-\-highlight-hunk
Visually highlight the hunk region before animating it. The highlight
is shown for
.B \-\-highlight-duration-ms
milliseconds, then cleared.

.TP
.BI \-\-highlight-color\  COLOR
Vim highlight group for hunk highlighting. Default:
.BR DiffChange .
Also:
.BR DiffAdd ,
.BR DiffDelete ,
.BR Search ,
.BR Visual ,
.BR IncSearch .

.TP
.BI \-\-highlight-duration-ms\  N
Highlight duration in milliseconds. Default: 1000.

.TP
.BI \-\-highlight-min-chars\  N
Minimum changed chars to trigger hunk highlighting. Default: 10.
Hunks with fewer changed chars are animated without highlighting.

.TP
.B \-\-fold-unchanged
Fold unchanged regions between hunks so the user only sees the changes.
Press
.B f
during animation to toggle folding on/off.

.TP
.BR \-\-theme\  dark | light | high-contrast
Color scheme for animation highlights:
.RS
.TP 4
.B dark
Set background=dark
.TP 4
.B light
Set background=light
.TP 4
.B high-contrast
Vivid green/red/yellow diff highlights
.RE

.SS Utility Options

.TP
.B \-\-no-tmux
(diffvim.pl only) Run vim directly in the terminal (no tmux wrapper).
Simpler single-shot use, but no FIFO-based user input.

.TP
.B \-\-remote
(diffvim.pl only) Use
.B vim \-\-remote-send
with
.B \-\-servername
instead of tmux send-keys. Eliminates tmux race conditions.

.TP
.B \-\-dry-run
Compute and print the diff ops without launching vim. Useful for
debugging parser issues.

.TP
.B \-\-diff\  FILE
Accept a unified diff/patch file as input instead of requiring two files.
Use
.B \-
for stdin. Enables:
.B git diff | diffvim \-\-diff \-

.TP
.B \-\-parser-compare
(diffvim.pl only) Run both parsers and report any differences in the
computed hunks. Exit code 0 if all match, 1 if any mismatch.

.TP
.B \-\-debug
Enable verbose logging of all Ex commands sent, with timestamps, to
.BR /tmp/diffvim-debug.log .
Useful for debugging race conditions and timing issues.

.TP
.BR \-\-version ,\  \-V
Print version, parser info, and dependency versions (vim, tmux, perl,
diff2html).

.TP
.BR \-\-help ,\  \-h
Show help message and exit.

.TP
.B \-\-auto-precompute
Automatically run the external compute tool (default: C, set via
.B DIFFVIM_COMPUTE_TOOL
or
.B \-\-compute-tool
) and use a temp file for
.B \-\-precomputed
without having to manually specify the file path.

.TP
.BI \-\-compute-tool\  c|cpp|rust|go
Which external compute tool to use with
.BR \-\-auto-precompute .
Default: c.

.TP
.B \-\-preset NAME
Apply a named preset that sets multiple options at once. Available
presets: fast-delete, review, present, ai-code, custom. Multiple
presets can be comma-separated. Also settable via
.B DIFFVIM_PRESET
environment variable. The custom preset reads options from
.BR DIFFVIM_PRESET_CUSTOM .

.TP
.B \-\-left-to-right
(Default: on) Sort ops within each line so deletes and inserts go from
left to right. Use
.B \-\-no-left-to-right
to disable.

.TP
.B \-\-word-accel
When inserting or deleting a word character by character, start slowly
and accelerate, then pause slightly. Total time equals uniform
char-by-char. Deletion is 20% faster by default (configurable via
.BR \-\-word-accel-delete-pct ).

.TP
.B \-\-rapid-identical-chars
Accelerate deletion of identical character runs (e.g. \-\-\-\-\-\-\-)
exponentially. Options:
.B \-\-rapid-identical-min
(default: 5),
.B \-\-rapid-identical-accel
(default: 50, lower=faster).

.TP
.B \-\-no-log-timing
Disable timing parameter info in log output. By default, all timing
parameters are included in the log.

.SH CONTROLS
During animation, the following keys are active in vim normal mode:

.SS Basic Controls
.TP
.B <Space>
Pause / resume the animation. In
.B \-\-step-mode ,
advances one char op instead.
.TP
.B n
Skip current hunk: apply all remaining character operations instantly,
then pause for review. Press
.B n
again to advance to the next hunk. This is the "review mode" \(em apply
one hunk at a time, pausing between each.
.TP
.B b
Back to previous hunk: revert the buffer to the state before the
current hunk started and replay it from the beginning.
.TP
.B q
Stop the animation. By default the buffer is then marked as not modified
so
.B :q
quits cleanly. Use
.B \-\-keep-dirty
to require
.B :q!
instead.

.SS Speed Controls
.TP
.B +
Speed up: multiply the current speed by 1.5.
.TP
.B \-
Slow down: divide the current speed by 1.5.
.TP
.B =
Reset speed to 1.0x.

.SS Multi-File Navigation
.TP
.B ]
Next file (in multi-file mode). Applies all remaining hunks instantly
and loads the next file pair.
.TP
.B [
Previous file (in multi-file mode). Loads the previous file pair.

.SS Granular Navigation
.TP
.B B
(Shift-B) Go back one char op.
.TP
.B N
(Shift-N) Skip to next file (multi-file mode).
.TP
.B Ctrl-B
Go back to the beginning.
.TP
.B Ctrl-N
Skip to the end.

.SS Undo/Redo
.TP
.B u
Undo last hunk (revert to previous snapshot).
.TP
.B Ctrl-r
Redo hunk.

.SS Display
.TP
.B ?
Toggle full-screen help overlay.
.TP
.B f
Toggle fold on/off (with
.BR \-\-fold-unchanged ).

.SS Progress
A progress message is shown in the vim status line:
.RS
.PP
.nf
diffvim: hunk 3/7 (42%) | speed 2.3x | PAUSED
.fi
.RE

.SH ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
All timing values can be set via environment variables. Command-line
options override environment variables, which override built-in defaults.

.TP
.B DIFFVIM_TICK_MS
Animation frame interval in milliseconds (default: 16, ~60fps).
.TP
.B DIFFVIM_TYPE_DELAY_MS
Delay between typed characters in milliseconds (default: 50).
.TP
.B DIFFVIM_DELETE_DELAY_MS
Delay between deleted characters in milliseconds (default: 40).
.TP
.B DIFFVIM_MOVE_MIN_MS
Minimum cursor glide duration in milliseconds (default: 250).
.TP
.B DIFFVIM_MOVE_MAX_MS
Maximum cursor glide duration in milliseconds (default: 1600).
.TP
.B DIFFVIM_MOVE_MS_PER_UNIT
Milliseconds per unit of glide distance (default: 6). Lines are weighted
80x more than columns.
.TP
.B DIFFVIM_HUNK_PAUSE_MS
Pause between hunks in milliseconds (default: 250).
.TP
.B DIFFVIM_WORD_PAUSE_MS
Pause after instant word in milliseconds (default: 150).
.TP
.B DIFFVIM_RAPID_EOL_DELAY_MS
Delay for rapid end-of-line deletion in milliseconds (default: 80).
Only relevant when
.B \-\-rapid-eol-delete
is on (which is the default).
.TP
.B DIFFVIM_RAPID_EOL_MIN_CHARS
Minimum trailing characters to trigger rapid EOL deletion (default: 3).
.TP
.B DIFFVIM_SPEED
Speed multiplier (default: 1.0). Same as
.BR \-\-speed .
.TP
.B DIFFVIM_MAX_LINE_LEN
Warn threshold for long lines (default: 10000).
.TP
.B DIFFVIM_HIGHLIGHT_COLOR
Highlight group for
.B \-\-highlight-hunk
(default: DiffChange).
.TP
.B DIFFVIM_HIGHLIGHT_DURATION_MS
Highlight duration in ms (default: 1000).
.TP
.B DIFFVIM_HIGHLIGHT_MIN_CHARS
Min changed chars to trigger highlight (default: 10).
.TP
.B DIFFVIM_KEEP_DIRTY
Set to
.B 1
to leave the buffer modified after animation; vim will then refuse
.B :q
and require
.BR :q! .
Default: unset (buffer is marked not modified, so
.B :q
works).
.TP
.B DIFFVIM_HIGHLIGHT_WORD_COLOR
Highlight group for
.B \-\-highlight-word
(default: Search).
.TP
.B DIFFVIM_HIGHLIGHT_WORD_DURATION_MS
Word highlight duration in ms (default: 300).
.TP
.B DIFFVIM_HIGHLIGHT_WORD_MIN_CHARS
Min word length to trigger highlight (default: 2).

.SH EXAMPLES

.SS Basic Usage
.PP
.nf
diffvim old.py new.py
.fi

.SS Speed Control
.PP
.nf
# Half speed for a presentation
diffvim \-\-speed 0.5 old.py new.py

# 3x speed for quick review
diffvim \-\-speed 3 old.py new.py
.fi

.SS Output
.PP
.nf
# Write result to file and quit
diffvim \-\-output result.py old.py new.py
.fi

.SS Display Options
.PP
.nf
# Center cursor, highlight hunks, fold unchanged regions
diffvim \-\-scroll zz \-\-highlight-hunk \-\-fold-unchanged old.py new.py

# High-contrast theme
diffvim \-\-theme high-contrast old.py new.py
.fi

.SS Diff Algorithms
.PP
.nf
# Use patience diff for more human-readable hunks
diffvim \-\-algorithm patience old.py new.py

# Word-level diff
diffvim \-\-word-diff old.py new.py

# Semantic cleanup
diffvim \-\-semantic-cleanup old.py new.py
.fi

.SS Word Batching
.PP
.nf
# Sequences > 5 chars are applied in one shot with a pause
diffvim \-\-max-word-chars 5 old.py new.py
.fi

.SS Rapid End-of-Line Deletion
.PP
.nf
# Default behavior: trailing line deletes applied in one rapid shot
diffvim old.py new.py

# Disable rapid EOL (delete one char at a time)
diffvim \-\-no-rapid-eol-delete old.py new.py

# Tune rapid EOL timing
diffvim \-\-rapid-eol-delay-ms 50 \-\-rapid-eol-min-chars 5 old.py new.py
.fi

.SS Buffer State After Animation
.PP
.nf
# Default: ':q' quits cleanly (buffer marked not modified)
diffvim old.py new.py

# Keep buffer modified; ':q!' required to quit
diffvim \-\-keep-dirty old.py new.py
.fi

.SS Word Highlighting
.PP
.nf
# Highlight the word at cursor before each change
diffvim \-\-highlight-word old.py new.py

# Use Visual group, 500ms duration, highlight words of 3+ chars
diffvim \-\-highlight-word \\
  \-\-highlight-word-color Visual \\
  \-\-highlight-word-duration-ms 500 \\
  \-\-highlight-word-min-chars 3 \\
  old.py new.py
.fi

.SS Multi-file Animation
.PP
.nf
diffvim \-\-multi old1.py:new1.py old2.py:new2.py
.fi

.SS Git Integration
.PP
.nf
# Replay last 5 commits of a file
diffvim \-\-replay src/main.py

# Specific commit range
diffvim \-\-replay src/main.py \-\-from v1.0 \-\-to HEAD

# Using \-\-git-rev syntax
diffvim \-\-git-rev HEAD~3..HEAD src/main.py

# Show git blame during animation
diffvim \-\-git-blame old.py new.py
.fi

.SS Unified Diff Input
.PP
.nf
# Animate from a patch file
diffvim \-\-diff my.patch

# From stdin
git diff | diffvim \-\-diff \-
.fi

.SS Debugging
.PP
.nf
# Dry run (print ops without launching vim)
diffvim \-\-dry-run old.py new.py

# Verbose logging
diffvim \-\-debug old.py new.py
cat /tmp/diffvim-debug.log

# Compare parsers
diffvim \-\-parser-compare old.py new.py
.fi

.SS Vim Plugin
.PP
.nf
# Inside an existing vim session:
:Diffvim old.py new.py
:Diffvim old.py new.py tabnew
.fi

